    ],
    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Paul Anthony Novelly, known as Tony, was an American businessman who built his fortune through Apex Oil, a petroleum trading, storage and distribution business. He joined the company as an employee, became an owner and guided it through bankruptcy. His interests also included oil terminals, specialty chemicals, property and a Michigan resort.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Working in a grocery store helped future oil businessman Tony Novelly pay for his education. He progressed from bagging groceries to customer-service management while studying finance at Saint Louis University. After graduation, he joined Shell, but later declined a promotion requiring a move to New York because he wanted to return to his family in St. Louis.\n\nEducation became a focus of his giving through the Horatio Alger Association. He helped finance scholarships across the United States and sponsored a programme for students in Quebec in honour of Brian Mulroney. He also helped establish an endowment supporting scholarships throughout Canada.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 92,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Primary member biography documents work and education; the association's anniversary history independently details his scholarship sponsorship and endowment work."
    },
    "source_ids": [
