      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 100,
    "html": "<p>Working in a grocery store helped future oil businessman Tony Novelly pay for his education. He progressed from bagging groceries to customer-service management while studying finance at Saint Louis University. After graduation, he joined Shell, but later declined a promotion requiring a move to New York because he wanted to return to his family in St. Louis.</p>\r\n<p>Education became a focus of his giving through the Horatio Alger Association. He helped finance scholarships across the United States and sponsored a programme for students in Quebec in honour of Brian Mulroney. He also helped establish an endowment supporting scholarships throughout Canada.</p>\r\n"
  },
